{"id":"95d06fa2c54b0d9c","group":"67","path":"67/67-thm-sigma-conservativity-separation.md","title":"Sigma Conservativity Does Not Detect a Disjunction","display":"thm-sigma-conservativity-separation — Sigma Conservativity Does Not Detect a Disjunction","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-thm-sigma-conservativity-separation","aliases":["67-thm-sigma-conservativity-separation"],"display":"thm-sigma-conservativity-separation — Sigma Conservativity Does Not Detect a Disjunction","depends_on":["[[67-df-partially-conservative]]","[[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]","[[67-df-PA]]","[[67-df-prim-provability]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf","source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_chapter":5,"source_label":"Theorem 5.5(a)","source_printed_pages":[67,68],"source_pdf_pages":[78,79],"verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"source statement and printed argument checked; full auxiliary formalization not independently reconstructed","eligible_as_verified_dependency":false},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-thm-sigma-conservativity-separation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-thm-sigma-conservativity-separation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-sigma-conservativity-separation — Sigma Conservativity Does Not Detect a Disjunction"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5d04e3c8a5885c18\" href=\"?note=5d04e3c8a5885c18\" title=\"67-df-partially-conservative\">67-df-partially-conservative</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"cd051851df5d2aa2\" href=\"?note=cd051851df5d2aa2\" title=\"67-df-PA\">67-df-PA</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"573b4c635ea6d91f\" href=\"?note=573b4c635ea6d91f\" title=\"67-df-prim-provability\">67-df-prim-provability</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"5"},{"key":"source_label","html":"Theorem 5.5(a)"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67</span><span>68</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>78</span><span>79</span></div>"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source statement and printed argument checked; full auxiliary formalization not independently reconstructed"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"false"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}\">\\(T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}\\)</span> 是一致的固定原始递归算术公理呈示，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\ge1\">\\(n\\ge1\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n,\\Pi_n\">\\(\\Sigma_n,\\Pi_n\\)</span> 及相对公式类取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\">\\(\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\\)</span> 为算术句子集；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vdash\">\\(\\vdash\\)</span> 为 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"573b4c635ea6d91f\" href=\"?note=573b4c635ea6d91f\" title=\"67-df-prim-provability\">67-df-prim-provability</a> 的元语言有限可推导性。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_n}\">\\(\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_n}\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"5d04e3c8a5885c18\" href=\"?note=5d04e3c8a5885c18\" title=\"67-df-partially-conservative\">67-df-partially-conservative</a>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\exists\\psi_0,\\psi_1\\in\\Sigma_n\\cap\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\\;\\left[\\left(T\\vdash\\neg(\\psi_0\\land\\psi_1)\\right)\\land\\left(T\\nvdash\\psi_0\\lor\\psi_1\\right)\\land\\bigwedge_{i&lt;2}\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_n}\\left(\\psi_i,T\\cup\\{\\neg\\psi_{1-i}\\}\\right)\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\exists\\psi_0,\\psi_1\\in\\Sigma_n\\cap\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\\;\\left[\\left(T\\vdash\\neg(\\psi_0\\land\\psi_1)\\right)\\land\\left(T\\nvdash\\psi_0\\lor\\psi_1\\right)\\land\\bigwedge_{i&lt;2}\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_n}\\left(\\psi_i,T\\cup\\{\\neg\\psi_{1-i}\\}\\right)\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>对应印刷67–68页/PDF78–79页定理5(a)。它给出上一原子中 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi_n\">\\(\\Pi_n\\)</span> 换为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n\">\\(\\Sigma_n\\)</span> 后的反例，不是仅重述两个句子的不可证性。</p>\n<p>已核对页面图像及引理6的双重自指证明结构：两个句子互斥；各自对另句否定之上的理论保持 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi_n\">\\(\\Pi_n\\)</span> 后果；析取仍不被 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> 证明。源引理6需要同时控制两公式的部分真近似与编码自指，当前未独立重建整条证明链，故仅记录来源陈述与证明阅读，不作已核验证明依赖。第7章区间非对偶性的书面证明实际使用更强的定理5(b)，不能用此(a)项冒充它的完整依赖。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-partially-conservative","status":"resolved","id":"5d04e3c8a5885c18","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-partially-conservative]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-arithmetical-classes","status":"resolved","id":"851cd80e64893935","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-PA","status":"resolved","id":"cd051851df5d2aa2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-PA]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-prim-provability","status":"resolved","id":"573b4c635ea6d91f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-prim-provability]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-arithmetical-classes","status":"resolved","id":"851cd80e64893935","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}$ 是一致的固定原始递归算术公理呈示，$n\\ge1$；$\\Sigma_n,\\Pi_n$ 及相对公式类取 [[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]。","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-prim-provability","status":"resolved","id":"573b4c635ea6d91f","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}$ 为算术句子集；$\\vdash$ 为 [[67-df-prim-provability]] 的元语言有限可推导性。","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-partially-conservative","status":"resolved","id":"5d04e3c8a5885c18","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_n}$ 采用 [[67-df-partially-conservative]]。","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}","display":false},{"tex":"n\\ge1","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma_n,\\Pi_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}","display":false},{"tex":"\\vdash","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Pi_n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\exists\\psi_0,\\psi_1\\in\\Sigma_n\\cap\\mathrm{Sent}_